{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-16T07:39:25Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm focusing on the most efficient tool utilization. It's becoming clearer that prioritizing specific tools will drastically improve my problem-solving ability. The goal is to always select the tool best suited for the immediate task at hand, regardless of how broad a command may be. This will keep work on the project organized.\n\n\n**Investigating Shader Loading**\n\nI'm now investigating why the `loadShader` function returned undefined. Recalling critical instructions, I am applying the rules for tool usage. It seems the problem lies in the p5.js setup. It requires a WEBGL context to load shaders, or there may be an issue with the function. Further investigation is needed to ensure the WEBGL context is initialized correctly and that the function is being called appropriately.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"\\\"p5.js\\\" \\\"loadShader\\\" returns undefined\"","toolAction":"\"Searching for loadShader undefined\"","toolSummary":"\"Search loadShader undefined\""}}]}
{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"SEARCH_WEB","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-16T07:39:34Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-16T10:39:34+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-16T10:39:37+03:00\nThe search for \"\"p5.js\" \"loadShader\" returns undefined\" returned the following summary:\nIf `loadShader` is returning `undefined` in your p5.js sketch, it is almost certainly because the function is being called outside of the `preload()` block, or the shader files are failing to load due to path/syntax issues.\n\nBecause `loadShader` is an asynchronous function that fetches external files, p5.js requires it to be used within `preload()` to ensure the shader is fully loaded before the rest of your sketch begins[1][2][3].\n\n### Common Causes & Solutions\n\n#### 1. Move `loadShader` to `preload()`\nIf you are calling `loadShader()` inside `setup()` or `draw()`, the variable will be `undefined` when your sketch first tries to use it because the file hasn't finished loading yet.\n\n**Incorrect:**\n```javascript\nfunction setup() {\n  createCanvas(400, 400, WEBGL);\n  myShader = loadShader('shader.vert', 'shader.frag'); // Too late!\n}\n```\n\n**Correct:**\n```javascript\nlet myShader;\n\nfunction preload() {\n  // Load here so p5.js waits until it's ready\n  myShader = loadShader('assets/shader.vert', 'assets/shader.frag');\n}\n\nfunction setup() {\n  createCanvas(400, 400, WEBGL);\n}\n\nfunction draw() {\n  shader(myShader);\n  // ... rest of your code\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Check File Paths\nIf the paths to your `.vert` and `.frag` files are incorrect, `loadShader` will fail to return a valid object.\n*   **Verify the directory:** Ensure your files are in the directory referenced in your code (e.g., if your files are in an `assets/` folder, make sure that folder exists in your project structure)[4].\n*   **Browser Console:** Open your browser's Developer Tools (F12) and check the **Console** tab. If the files failed to load, you will likely see a 404 error indicating the path is wrong.\n\n#### 3. Shader Syntax Errors\nIf the shader file itself contains a syntax error (in GLSL), the compilation may fail. \n*   Check the console for messages like `ERROR: 0:1: '...' : syntax error`[5][4]\n<truncated 231 bytes>\nmode[1][6]. Ensure your `createCanvas` call includes this argument:\n```javascript\ncreateCanvas(windowWidth, windowHeight, WEBGL);\n```\n\n### Debugging Tip\nIf you are still having trouble, you can use the optional callback parameters to see if the loading process is succeeding or failing[1]:\n\n```javascript\nfunction preload() {\n  myShader = loadShader('shader.vert', 'shader.frag', \n    () => console.log('Shader loaded successfully!'),\n    (err) => console.error('Failed to load shader:', err)\n  );\n}\n```\nThis will tell you immediately if the issue is a file-not-found error or a deeper compilation issue[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [p5js.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFciLZGcnXajQrDeMYAAB4ncBaPrO5snAM5SdfJFICrWJpLUtT8eIrEpsB_2U4cHqzbRIvtxk_IlrRWN8qejk8splqserttTtL7XZbD1pWBBNPnfhhKczeVrA56Y2zgrA==)\n[2] [docs.rs](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFFpqX56SFvMqw8zGswf5HE_lQF-hhygJ6zp53wdzWH9TdWRBRf5P4jltUr_jMAXxsK7blqQw86nNuXo_qLFsLugL6C5eIR0YD0w_b83s7PKEAW9g20v7ggptwQ4hr8yCxCrv7ejVxSbvqA7_a5)\n[3] [processing.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFzDwimbdl4XlzuCDY-dLxtMnrfkC_VW6IzEZzEOgfPuO-ld0SGXV45Z9oY0IIidYesjPY7jufh8CB81ppLtJ-eYzCYXDZO3o_L59sebn4BNSkHDu66163MscTsgOQDyKh6u9L1iHRRiKULteK0nAUBbkh0ACul7NI2nxX9_JvxbCnC-aTOZ-eeLCbY)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFMRWNSLHaF4RThvMpN1SI3l-5KZj0bQyhTRc3YQ-KHs85FJtGRfY4b8AVamryioa3DOD9F3_UZPeaV9z5sq1JItTphiVGtFucZVEVC4-wFpRI5sEIRM_J8BCjkgnm0dN38UTGeVA==)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFMRWNSLHaF4RThvMpN1SI3l-5KZj0bQyhTRc3YQ-KHs85FJtGRfY4b8AVamryioa3DOD9F3_UZPeaV9